  "limitations": [
    "Every structure here is a prediction. ESMFold returns coordinates for any sequence it accepts, and a confident-looking fold of a domain cut out of its chain is still a model of that domain in isolation.",
    "A domain folded alone has lost whatever its neighbours contributed to its shape. The per-residue confidence is the only guide to that here, and it is the model's own opinion rather than an independent check.",
    "The sequences are reconstructed from the genome and the relative's annotated ranges rather than read from the chain record, which deletes them. The reconstruction is the same alignment the chain stage runs, but it is a second computation of the same thing and could differ from the recorded run if the reference entry has been curated since.",
    "`runs/folded_structure/mpro_nsp5.pdb` is untouched. The main protease is folded again here, separately, so the committed artifact this repository reproduces byte for byte is not disturbed by this module."
  ],
